Why this package uses `3.0 (native)` (see `debian/source/format`).

This project is its own upstream: releases are cut from this repository
(`v*` tags drive `.github/workflows/release.yml`), and the `.deb` is
built directly from the tagged tree in CI
(`.github/workflows/build-packages.yml` stamps `debian/changelog` at
release time). There is no separate upstream tarball, and the version
string carries no Debian revision suffix that quilt mode would split
off into a `.orig` / `.debian.tar` pair.

Switching to `3.0 (quilt)` would therefore require manufacturing a
`.orig` tarball in CI purely to satisfy the format, with no change in
what actually ships. `native` is kept deliberately; revisit only if a
genuinely separate upstream release artifact exists one day.
